// NEGATIVE-TEST FIXTURE (not a real Cerise component; never staged into any
// product). A virtual machine monitor that is NOT the one the lint permits.
//
// The over-privilege lint grants exactly two (component, protocol) pairs to the
// VMM — `cryogen_vmm` + fuchsia.kernel.HypervisorResource, and `cryogen_vmm` +
// fuchsia.kernel.VmexResource — and it matches the component name with `==`
// rather than `starts_with`, precisely so that a second, differently-named VMM
// cannot inherit the grant by sharing a prefix. This fixture is that second VMM:
// its meta-name is `cryogen_vmm_v2`, which a `starts_with` check would admit
// silently and an `==` check must reject.
//
// It therefore proves two things at once, and both are load-bearing:
//   * the lint is not vacuous for the two newly-permitted protocols (before this
//     fixture existed, `route_check/tests/negative.rs` covered only
//     fuchsia.kernel.MmioResource, so the two new allowlist entries would have
//     shipped with no red control at all);
//   * the exactness of the match is enforced rather than merely commented.
{
    program: { runner: "elf", binary: "bin/cryogen_vmm_v2" },
    use: [
        { protocol: "fuchsia.logger.LogSink" },
        { protocol: "fuchsia.kernel.HypervisorResource" },
        { protocol: "fuchsia.kernel.VmexResource" },
    ],
}
